<p>Mexican navy special forces arrested Audias Flores Silva, known as “El Jardinero,” in Nayarit on Monday, April 27, in an operation against the Jalisco New Generation Cartel, or CJNG. Security Secretary Omar García Harfuch said Flores had an arrest warrant in Mexico and was wanted by U.S. authorities for extradition; the United States had offered a $5 million reward for information leading to his arrest. Officials and reports described Flores as a regional commander on Mexico’s Pacific coast and a possible successor to CJNG founder Nemesio Oseguera, known as “El Mencho,” who was killed in a security operation in February. Later Monday, Mexican authorities also announced the arrest of César Alejandro “N,” known as “El Güero Conta,” in Zapopan, Jalisco; officials identified him as a financial operator for Flores.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/tyN2rxNsZFBoHItO9AmpodPdszpMEV_WUNPp0XklI0522-9bVWpskZO3jDZ0RQUlJvTMlLDvYoP93efFDsvEd6Aknn55hNOn17up3SbyfDnBb0hJQxGKQUbYmm2tjL9gJSVYYvhIM9ToEHm4Z_Jas6EsqsNilMeOM-MJSIMsejUxwRMnh445ScV1KfA0ybSaads98HFg7m6h9na1I18jsAZ2OOQ-LKyYfCLVOoYHXm7U9gPnONqYlXVW_GjnDWRm8Z2TMSi1fzF_2vDC' alt='Members of Mexican Special Forces escort Audias Flores, known as “El Jardinero,” in Nayarit, Mexico, in a handout distributed on April 27, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Operation scale: The navy said the operation followed 19 months of surveillance and involved more than 500 troops, six helicopters and several aircraft.</li><li>Resort proximity: Officials said the hideout was about 20km north of Puerto Vallarta, a popular resort city.</li><li>Escape attempt: Officials said Flores tried to hide in a drainage ditch after his escorts scattered to divert security forces.</li><li>Financial case: García Harfuch said César Alejandro “N” was accused of laundering illicit proceeds through companies and front people, including purchases of aircraft, boats, homes and ranches.</li></ul><blockquote>The operation was carried out with surgical precision without a single shot being fired - Mexican Navy</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Omar García Harfuch: Mexico’s security secretary said the Navy’s special forces planned, developed and carried out the operation. (<a href='https://www.elfinanciero.com.mx/nacional/2026/04/27/trancazo-al-cjng-detienen-a-audias-flores-silva-alias-el-jardinero-posible-sucesor-de-el-mencho/'>El Financiero</a>)</li><li>El País: The newspaper said the capture gave Mexico’s navy a boost after recent scrutiny over fuel-smuggling scandals and the interoceanic train accident. (<a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-04-28/mexico-deals-second-major-blow-to-jalisco-new-generation-cartel-in-just-two-months.html'>El País</a>)</li><li>David Saucedo: The security analyst told AFP that Flores had been El Mencho’s “right-hand man” and had negotiated on Oseguera’s behalf with Los Chapitos, citing U.S. and Mexican intelligence sources. (<a href='https://www.nacion.com/el-mundo/detienen-en-mexico-a-lider-narco-y-posible-sucesor/BMCWQFQHBZF25NUJO2C4UGRII4/story/'>La Nación</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/28/mexican-special-forces-arrest-top-commander-audias-flores-el-jardinero-of-powerful-cartel'>Mexican special forces arrest top commander of cartel and his alleged money launderer</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/mexicos-military-captures-top-cartel-leader-blow-jalisco-132441441'>Mexico&#x27;s military captures top cartel leader in blow to Jalisco New Generation</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/28/mexican-army-captures-top-cartel-boss-in-another-blow-to-jalisco-new-generation'>Mexican army captures top cartel boss in another blow to Jalisco New Generation</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-04-28/mexico-deals-second-major-blow-to-jalisco-new-generation-cartel-in-just-two-months.html'>Mexico